    ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
}
```
Reason:
This conditional check only decodes the second file status when the parent directories are different. If the source and destination directories are the same, the second status is not decoded, causing the xdr pointer to remain unchanged. This results in the volsync record being read incorrectly, leading to unreliable updates of the directory data version numbers.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
```
Reason:
By always decoding the second status regardless of whether the directories are the same or different, the xdr pointer is correctly advanced. This ensures that the volsync record is read accurately, allowing the directory data version numbers to be reliably updated based on the correct state of the destination directory.


